1264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 4055 0 R
/E (The mandatory up-to-60-day pause during sowing/harvest assumes that rural workers can absorb income loss by shifting into agricultural labour during this period. This assumption does not hold uniformly: a large share of MGNREGA workers, especially women, are landless and do not have alternative agricultural income during the pause. Since women account for close to 60% of person-days generated nationally under MGNREGA \(higher still in states like Kerala and Tamil Nadu\), the provision carries a disproportionate gender impact.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
