<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 528 0 R
/T (Issues with Poverty Estimation in India)
/E (Issues with Poverty Estimation in India)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1303 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 4086 0 R
/E (Multiplicity of Methodologies: India has witnessed a proliferation of different methodologies over the decades, ranging from calorie-based to expenditure-based thresholds. This leads to inconsistencies, making comparisons difficult and sometimes resulting in the adoption of less comprehensive criteria, thus underestimating poverty levels \(e.g., Rangarajan Committee methodology has not been implemented for official estimates\).)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1304 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 4087 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1305 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 4088 0 R
/E (Emphasis on Incidence, Neglect of Intensity: The headcount ratio \(HCR\) simply measures the proportion of people below the poverty line, failing to recognize the severity and depth \(intensity\) of deprivation among the poor. Thus, small pockets of severe poverty may be masked by generally low poverty rates.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 4089 0 R
/E (Mismatch with Ground Realities: Outdated consumption baskets, failure to account for inflation, and delays in data publication often result in estimates that do not reflect real-time poverty levels or the contemporary standard of living.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1307 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 4090 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1308 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 4091 0 R
/E (Technical and Governance Issues: Inadequate data publication timelines, informalisation of the economy, exclusion and inclusion errors \(such as ghost beneficiaries in BPL lists\), and political sensitivity around poverty figures further limit the reliability and impact of official poverty measures.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1309 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 4092 0 R
/E (Estimates Fail to Capture Dynamics: Seasonal or cyclical poverty, impacts of global disruptions like COVID-19, and rising inequality are not captured adequately through static poverty lines)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
